STEP 1 -- a 120-day lease is delivered as option 51 = 10,368,000 in OFFER and ACK    PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
tb277$ sudo -n python3.8 dhcp4.py client eth3 --mac 02:c4:00:00:01:01 \
         --prl 1,3,6,51,58,59 --arp-watch 192.168.10.0/24 --wait 20 \
         --pcap leg1-120d.pcap --json leg1-120d.json

  Every DHCP frame of the transaction, as decoded from the capture:
      DISCOVER  yiaddr=0.0.0.0          opt51=None       opt58=None  opt59=None
      OFFER     yiaddr=192.168.10.100   opt51=10368000   opt58=None  opt59=None
      REQUEST   yiaddr=0.0.0.0          opt51=None       opt58=None  opt59=None
      ACK       yiaddr=192.168.10.100   opt51=10368000   opt58=None  opt59=None
                                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ 10,368,000 s = 120 d 0 h 0 m 0 s,
                                                       in BOTH the OFFER and the ACK

  --- summary ---
  chaddr 02:c4:00:00:01:01 xid 0x6b211f9f
  sent: 1 DISCOVER, 1 REQUEST
  OFFER: 192.168.10.100
     lease_time=10368000
  ACK  : ACK 192.168.10.100
     lease_time=10368000 renewal=None rebinding=None

  Corroboration from the DUT, read AFTER the frames:
awplus# show clock
  UTC Time:   Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:33:57 +0000
  Timezone: UTC
  Timezone Offset: +00:00
  Summer time zone: None
awplus# show ip dhcp binding
  Pool CKPOOL Network 192.168.10.0/24
  DHCP Client Entries
  IP Address      ClientId                            Type    Expiry
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  192.168.10.100  02c4.0000.0101                      Dynamic 12 Feb 2027 02:33:39

  => STEP 1 PASS: the configured 120-day lease reaches the client as option 51 =
     10,368,000 s in both the OFFER and the ACK, and the DUT's own binding table agrees --
     granted 15 Oct 2026 02:33:39 UTC, expiring 12 Feb 2027 02:33:39 UTC, which is
     16 + 30 + 31 + 31 + 12 = 120 days, to the second. That expiry is only readable because
     the DUT's RTC was repaired before the run. Options 58 and 59 are absent although
     option 55 asked for them; recorded, not required (see CAVEAT).

STEP 2 -- the boundary: 120 is accepted, 121 and 999 are refused                     PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: sent through tools/ckcon.py rather than the stop-on-error config driver, so that
  the refusals are CAPTURED as the expected result instead of aborting the batch.

awplus(config)# ip dhcp pool CKPOOL
awplus(dhcp-config)# lease 121 0 0
                                ^
  % Invalid input detected at '^' marker.          <-- 121 days refused by the parser
awplus(dhcp-config)# lease 120 0 0
awplus(dhcp-config)#                               <-- 120 days accepted silently, no "% "
awplus(dhcp-config)# lease 999 0 0
                                ^
  % Invalid input detected at '^' marker.          <-- far beyond the ceiling, refused
awplus(dhcp-config)# end

  => STEP 2 PASS: the parser accepts exactly up to 120 days and refuses 121 and 999, so the
     documented range (lease.md, "<days> ... from 0 to 120") holds on
     sin_x96056-20261012-24 and the old 30-day IP Infusion ceiling is gone. The accepted
     and refused values differ by one day on the same command on the same pool, so this is
     the ceiling itself and not a general parser limit. This step is the feature: the
     enhancement is the raised maximum.

STEP 3 -- other lease values must yield their own option 51, in the same run         PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: three successive IN-PLACE changes with no `no lease` between them, so each
  overwrites a live value, each followed by a fresh client and graded on the captured
  OFFER and ACK.

awplus(dhcp-config)# lease 1 0 0     then  lease 0 1 0     then  lease 120 0 0

  | configured      | expected opt51 | measured OFFER | measured ACK | chaddr            |
  | --------------- | -------------- | -------------- | ------------ | ----------------- |
  | lease 1 0 0     |         86,400 |         86,400 |       86,400 | 02:c4:00:00:01:02 |
  | lease 0 1 0     |          3,600 |          3,600 |        3,600 | 02:c4:00:00:01:03 |
  | lease 120 0 0   |     10,368,000 |     10,368,000 |   10,368,000 | 02:c4:00:00:01:04 |

  (addresses allocated in order: .101, .102, .103 respectively)

  => STEP 3 PASS: every configured value matched exactly, in both messages. The 1-day row
     is the control the 120-day claim rests on -- identical crafted DISCOVER, identical
     pool, identical cabling, and only the configured lease differs, yet option 51 moves
     with it. The 1-hour row adds a third point, so the result is a curve rather than a
     two-point coincidence, and it proves sub-day granularity. Each change was an in-place
     overwrite of a live value and each took effect on the wire immediately, with
     `show ip dhcp pool` agreeing with the wire at every point: there is no silent discard
     of a repeated `lease` command on this platform.

STEP 4 -- removal: `no lease` restores the 1-day default and clears the config       PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
awplus(config)# ip dhcp pool CKPOOL
awplus(dhcp-config)# no lease
awplus# show ip dhcp pool
  Pool CKPOOL :
    subscriber-id substitution for client-id is not enabled
    network: 192.168.10.0/24
    address ranges:
      addr: 192.168.10.100 to 192.168.10.110
    lease <days:hours:minutes:seconds> <1:0:0:0>   <-- the documented default
    subnet mask: 255.255.255.0 (pool's network mask)

  Proven on the wire, not only in the show -- fresh chaddr:
  --- summary ---
  chaddr 02:c4:00:00:01:05 xid 0xa7854bbd
  sent: 1 DISCOVER, 1 REQUEST
  OFFER: 192.168.10.104
     lease_time=86400
  ACK  : ACK 192.168.10.104
     lease_time=86400 renewal=None rebinding=None

awplus# show running-config
  ...
  ip dhcp pool CKPOOL
   network 192.168.10.0 255.255.255.0
   range 192.168.10.100 192.168.10.110
  !
  ...                                              <-- the lease line is GONE

  => STEP 4 PASS: `no lease` is not merely a reset of the displayed value -- the next real
     client is handed option 51 = 86,400 s, and the lease line has disappeared from the
     running-config rather than being rewritten as `lease 1 0 0`. Removal is complete in
     both the configuration and the behaviour.

